WEBVTT

00:01.040 --> 00:02.350
<i>All right.</i>

00:02.850 --> 00:06.900
<i>Time to make a sign language 
guide for Itsuomi-san!</i>

00:10.690 --> 00:15.870
<i>The day I realized that 
the emotion I felt for him was love...</i>

00:16.030 --> 00:18.370
If you want to learn sign language,
I can teach you

00:16.030 --> 00:18.370
<b></b>Notes

00:18.700 --> 00:21.660
Ooh... Thanks.

00:23.420 --> 00:27.040
<i>It'd be nice if I could hand it to him 
when I visit the bar with Rin-chan.</i>

00:27.040 --> 00:29.120
<i>But I need to figure out the right time.</i>

00:29.120 --> 00:31.580
<i>If it seems like a bother, 
I'll put it away immediately.</i>

00:32.440 --> 00:33.130
<i>Huh?</i>

00:33.130 --> 00:37.140
<b>Thank you</b>

00:33.940 --> 00:37.140
<i>Drawing sign language 
is harder than I expected.</i>

00:37.620 --> 00:39.990
<i>The right hand goes like this, so...</i>

00:40.530 --> 00:41.640
<i>Hmm?</i>

00:42.050 --> 00:43.210
Yuki!

00:43.210 --> 00:44.910
Sorry, but could you go get...

00:45.890 --> 00:48.180
That's a peculiar dance.

02:21.010 --> 02:22.490
Hello!

02:22.840 --> 02:25.880
Welcome. Have a seat wherever you like.

02:25.880 --> 02:27.000
Thank you.

02:27.290 --> 02:30.650
<i>Rin-chan's less nervous than last time.</i>

02:31.320 --> 02:33.880
<i>Meanwhile, I'm way more tense.</i>

02:51.680 --> 02:53.050
It's ringing.

02:55.480 --> 02:57.280
What's that noise?

02:57.440 --> 02:59.780
<b>The hearing aids give off feedback
when they're not worn snugly</b>

03:00.110 --> 03:01.850
Huh...

03:01.850 --> 03:04.660
Happens during class sometimes, too.

03:04.950 --> 03:07.240
<b>How much can you hear right now?</b>

03:08.260 --> 03:11.770
<i>I've never heard actual sounds before...</i>

03:12.670 --> 03:15.000
<b>It feels like all the sounds (?)
are mixed into one big mess</b>

03:15.170 --> 03:18.010
<b>I can't tell which sounds are coming from where, or what they are</b>

03:19.060 --> 03:20.330
From birth?

03:22.010 --> 03:24.640
<b>And I can't hear anything
when I take off my hearing aids</b>

03:29.140 --> 03:30.140
Hey!

03:30.460 --> 03:32.840
Sorry about Itsu and all his questions.

03:32.840 --> 03:34.920
Here, clean all this up.

03:34.920 --> 03:35.860
Sure.

03:36.920 --> 03:40.620
He always tries to get 
all up in people's business.

03:40.620 --> 03:44.030
Yeah, he does do that, doesn't he?

03:44.030 --> 03:46.660
<i>Is it interest? Or plain curiosity?</i>

03:47.020 --> 03:48.860
<i>It makes me happy either way.</i>

03:50.010 --> 03:53.420
I wonder if being born overseas 
has something to do with it.

03:53.420 --> 03:56.540
Who knows? I think Itsu's 
a little unique regardless.

03:59.300 --> 04:01.760
<b>Sign Language Guide</b>

04:00.290 --> 04:01.760
A sign language guide?

04:02.290 --> 04:04.640
Did you make that, Yuki-chan?

04:04.640 --> 04:07.740
Hey, can I see, too?

04:07.740 --> 04:08.390
Whoa!

04:08.390 --> 04:12.430
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

04:08.390 --> 04:12.430
<b>Note: These are
right-handed signs.
If you're left-handed,
flip these horizontally!

<u>Point!</u> It's recommended
to practice sign language
in front of a mirror!!</b>

04:08.800 --> 04:10.330
Oh, wow!

04:10.330 --> 04:13.200
That's so much info! Writing all this down 
must've been a lot of effort!

04:12.560 --> 04:15.150
<b>Finger Syllables Chart</b>

04:13.200 --> 04:15.150
The drawings are so cute!

04:15.480 --> 04:17.930
Great job, Yuki!

04:18.650 --> 04:20.320
My name...

04:20.320 --> 04:21.210
"I"...

04:22.240 --> 04:23.150
"Tsu"...

04:24.800 --> 04:26.160
I don't get it.

04:26.790 --> 04:28.080
Is this how you sign "tsu"?

04:28.080 --> 04:30.040
<i>Oh, "tsu" is...</i>

04:36.390 --> 04:39.840
<i>Itsuomi-san's fingers are so long.</i>

04:43.880 --> 04:47.430
Wow, you're as red as the souvenir 
I got you from Laos.

04:47.430 --> 04:48.680
<i>That thing?!</i>

04:49.400 --> 04:50.680
Thanks for this.

04:51.090 --> 04:53.290
Though I dunno if I'll use it.

04:53.290 --> 04:54.140
<i>What?!</i>

04:54.140 --> 04:55.560
I won't get it just with drawings.

04:56.440 --> 04:58.940
Teach me in person, Yuki.

05:00.360 --> 05:02.570
What signs do you use often?

05:03.070 --> 05:06.950
<b>Cute

Thank you</b>

05:04.440 --> 05:06.280
"Cute," huh?

05:08.360 --> 05:10.020
<i>Itsuomi-san's signing...</i>

05:10.710 --> 05:15.960
<i>It feels reassuring, like it'll embrace 
anything and everything in stride.</i>

05:25.330 --> 05:26.220
What's up?

05:28.220 --> 05:31.770
Oh. Sudden contact can make 
her jump, apparently.

05:31.770 --> 05:32.740
Huh?

05:32.740 --> 05:33.690
Sorry.

05:35.470 --> 05:37.930
<i>My heart is leaping out of my chest.</i>

05:37.930 --> 05:39.670
<i>I hope they can't hear it.</i>

05:39.150 --> 05:45.490
<b>It's okay if it's you,



Itsuomi-san</b>

05:40.880 --> 05:45.490
<i>There's a girl here who's 
madly in love with you.</i>

05:46.110 --> 05:51.350
<i>What should I do, 
now that I've fallen for you?</i>

05:53.980 --> 05:56.120
Yay!

05:57.320 --> 05:58.710
We're here.

05:59.100 --> 06:00.940
How long have you been barhopping?

06:00.940 --> 06:03.250
This is only our second one.

06:05.910 --> 06:07.170
Sorry about that.

06:07.680 --> 06:09.470
<i>That gave me a start.</i>

06:09.470 --> 06:12.050
You okay, Shinshin?

06:13.800 --> 06:16.830
Sowwy, did that stawtle you?

06:16.830 --> 06:17.390
<i>Whoa.</i>

06:18.260 --> 06:20.150
<i>This girl's pretty.</i>

06:20.610 --> 06:22.480
<i>Her hair's so silky.</i>

06:22.480 --> 06:26.480
What the... You're so pwetty, miss.

06:26.480 --> 06:28.900
You in the market for a hairstyle change?

06:28.900 --> 06:33.900
Y'see, he's a really good stylist.

06:33.900 --> 06:35.660
You're laying it on thick!

06:36.180 --> 06:40.080
<i>Okay... I have no idea what they're saying.</i>

06:40.080 --> 06:44.040
Short hair will probably look great on you.

06:44.390 --> 06:50.160
Or you could try a different color! 
Maybe some highlights, too?

06:50.160 --> 06:50.590
Shin.

06:51.410 --> 06:52.550
You're coming over here.

06:52.960 --> 06:54.000
You too, Emma.

06:54.000 --> 06:55.100
Okay!

06:56.470 --> 06:58.100
Sorry about that, Yuki.

06:58.540 --> 07:02.460
<i>Does he know him? Are they friends?</i>

06:59.570 --> 07:03.360
Take off your coats. And sit here.

07:03.830 --> 07:05.610
I'll have a beer, Itsu-kun.

07:05.610 --> 07:07.440
And I'll take a glass of red wine!

07:07.440 --> 07:09.430
All you're getting is water, you drunks.

07:09.000 --> 07:12.460
They're Itsu's classmates from high school.

07:09.840 --> 07:11.630
Don't want water.

07:11.630 --> 07:13.620
Red wine!

07:12.460 --> 07:13.620
Oh?

07:14.220 --> 07:16.330
Itsu-kun's such a meanie.

07:14.470 --> 07:18.950
The dude in the sunglasses is actually 
the cool, standoffish type when sober.

07:16.330 --> 07:21.140
Always acting like I'm some kind of alcoholic.
I'm not drunk at all, okay?

07:19.880 --> 07:22.780
<i>Alcohol can be scary, huh?</i>

07:24.130 --> 07:28.130
Hey, Itsu-kun, are you gonna be 
sticking around for a while?

07:28.130 --> 07:29.310
Why?

07:29.310 --> 07:31.130
I just wanna know!

07:31.480 --> 07:34.340
Why do you keep going 
abroad at the drop of a hat?

07:34.600 --> 07:36.950
<i>Huh? She was really clinging to him.</i>

07:37.350 --> 07:39.850
<i>I get that she may be drunk,</i>

07:40.530 --> 07:43.670
<i>but even then, the way she's looking at him...</i>

07:44.280 --> 07:47.180
Wha? Why now?!

07:47.180 --> 07:48.190
What's wrong?

07:48.190 --> 07:52.680
My mom just texted me, 
"I'm at your place, Rin."

07:52.680 --> 07:55.470
Sorry, Yuki, I gotta go.

07:55.470 --> 07:57.620
Yuki? Yuki?

07:58.450 --> 08:00.370
<i>What are they to each other?</i>

08:03.240 --> 08:05.430
Did you say you're from Fukuoka, Rin-chan?

08:05.950 --> 08:07.930
I couldn't tell from your accent at all.

08:07.930 --> 08:13.010
Well, I tried really hard to fix it 
over my first year here.

08:09.430 --> 08:11.130
<i>It's eating away at me.</i>

08:13.480 --> 08:15.140
<i>She's clinging to him again?!</i>

08:15.140 --> 08:17.120
Whoa, what's with them?

08:17.120 --> 08:17.900
Huh?

08:18.440 --> 08:20.100
Oh, Emma-chan?

08:20.720 --> 08:22.850
Are those two going out?

08:26.950 --> 08:30.140
They're not going out. Just friends.

08:30.540 --> 08:33.360
I don't think there's any chance they'll 
get together in the future, either.

08:33.360 --> 08:35.230
Huh? Why's that?

08:35.610 --> 08:38.660
That's not something I should be telling you.

08:39.360 --> 08:41.750
<i>Hearing that just makes me feel</i>

08:42.080 --> 08:46.250
<i>like their relationship is a special one.</i>

08:47.900 --> 08:48.870
Yuki-chan?

08:49.600 --> 08:52.750
I think he's serious about 
learning sign language.

08:52.750 --> 08:54.040
Teach him, okay?

08:54.040 --> 08:56.560
Kyou, where's the wine opener?

08:56.560 --> 08:57.990
Coming.

08:59.110 --> 09:01.270
Bye. Feel free to come back anytime.

09:04.930 --> 09:08.270
<i>"Be careful... on your way home."</i>

09:13.280 --> 09:17.860
<i>I should trust what the boss says 
about his relationship with that girl.</i>

09:17.860 --> 09:22.840
Man, I had a fun time 
chatting with him tonight!

09:22.840 --> 09:26.290
I gotta put my best foot forward so that 
things with Kyouya-san go smoothly.

09:26.290 --> 09:27.930
Right, Yuki?

09:32.510 --> 09:37.940
<i>At some point, my race had 
already begun. I just didn't know it.</i>

09:38.620 --> 09:42.890
<i>I should put my best foot 
forward, too. I want to.</i>

09:48.310 --> 09:51.320
I had lots of fun, too!
You two make the place
a lot brighter just with
your presence.
Hope you have a good
day at college tomorrow.

09:48.310 --> 09:51.320
Thank you, Kyouya-san!
Hope you have a good
day at work, too!

09:48.310 --> 09:51.320
<b>Good night</b>

09:48.310 --> 09:51.320
<b>Night~</b>

09:56.070 --> 09:59.320
Thanks for last night.
\hI'd be happy to teach
\h\hyou sign language
\h\hagain anytime.

09:56.070 --> 09:59.320
Sure

09:56.070 --> 09:59.320
Night

09:56.070 --> 09:59.320
Good night

10:31.830 --> 10:33.600
<i>It's been four days.</i>

10:33.600 --> 10:37.550
<i>I haven't texted Itsuomi-san or met him.</i>

10:37.550 --> 10:39.740
<i>Maybe he's overseas again.</i>

10:41.040 --> 10:42.570
<i>Or maybe...</i>

10:45.030 --> 10:46.630
<i>I won't let it eat away at me!</i>

10:49.370 --> 10:51.120
Night

10:49.370 --> 10:51.120
Good night

10:49.370 --> 10:51.120
Hello
Are you in Japan?

10:51.170 --> 10:52.130
Today

10:51.210 --> 10:52.130
Hello
Are you in Japan?

10:52.430 --> 10:54.220
<i>I texted him...</i>

10:54.220 --> 10:55.930
<i>I hope that was okay.</i>

10:57.880 --> 10:59.550
I'm at the laundromat
near college now

10:57.880 --> 10:59.580
<i>He replied instantly!</i>

10:59.550 --> 11:01.260
Want to meet up?
Or do you not?

11:06.600 --> 11:07.350
Oh?

11:09.760 --> 11:11.140
Are you going out?

11:11.840 --> 11:13.110
"For a bit"?

11:13.760 --> 11:15.770
Be home by curfew!

11:16.390 --> 11:19.610
<i>I have less than two hours.</i>

11:20.030 --> 11:23.870
<i>I've never met anyone out at this time.</i>

11:24.190 --> 11:25.610
<i>This is a first!</i>

11:28.910 --> 11:29.800
Hey!

11:29.800 --> 11:31.040
<i>Ow!</i>

11:31.910 --> 11:34.000
<i>Tissues? Why?</i>

11:34.000 --> 11:36.040
Where are you going at this hour?!

11:34.040 --> 11:37.800
<b>screeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee</b>

11:36.040 --> 11:37.800
<i>O-O-O-Oushi-kun?!</i>

11:39.250 --> 11:41.930
<i>I gotta go. See you.</i>

11:43.720 --> 11:46.520
<i>How many packs of tissues does he have?!</i>

11:46.520 --> 11:50.000
<i>What, you meeting someone right now?</i>

11:50.000 --> 11:51.690
<i>Yeah, why?</i>

11:53.570 --> 11:55.440
<i>It's not some guy, is it?</i>

11:56.870 --> 11:57.860
Wha?!

11:58.270 --> 12:01.120
<i>He called you out this late?</i>

12:01.120 --> 12:04.870
<i>I told my mom I'm going out. 
I'll be home by curfew, too.</i>

12:05.620 --> 12:07.870
Is it that silver-haired dude?

12:10.100 --> 12:12.490
<i>Meeting him alone is a bad idea.</i>

12:13.020 --> 12:16.540
<i>He's probably just having fun 
messing with you.</i>

12:16.540 --> 12:19.340
<i>Don't talk about him like that.</i>

12:20.470 --> 12:22.340
<i>If that ain't it...</i>

12:22.670 --> 12:25.840
He's just jerking himself off 
over how nice he is!

12:27.750 --> 12:30.600
<i>My race has already begun.</i>

12:31.120 --> 12:34.170
<i>And now that it has, I won't look back.</i>

13:11.120 --> 13:12.070
Want a drink?

13:12.550 --> 13:14.540
Oh, no need to pay me back.

13:17.570 --> 13:21.270
Yuki, do you have 10 yen on you? 
I want a drink, too.

13:21.900 --> 13:23.650
<b>Green Tea</b>

13:21.900 --> 13:23.650
<b>Hot</b>

13:25.280 --> 13:26.260
Thanks.

13:27.400 --> 13:29.670
Do you want this? Or do you not?

13:29.670 --> 13:31.280
Think it's worth around 10 yen.

13:31.780 --> 13:33.880
Can't really use it in Japan, though.

13:34.790 --> 13:36.290
<i>I've never seen this before.</i>

13:36.960 --> 13:39.160
<i>Which country is it from?</i>

13:40.040 --> 13:42.000
Kuna. I got it in Croatia

13:42.430 --> 13:45.300
Wanna see some others? Or do you not?

13:45.550 --> 13:49.470
You have more?

13:47.130 --> 13:49.470
I'd love to see!

13:49.300 --> 13:51.930
Well, I don't have any
on me right now

13:50.800 --> 13:51.930
But some other time, sure

13:55.680 --> 13:57.190
By the way

13:57.440 --> 14:00.190
Why do you go
overseas so often?

13:59.010 --> 14:00.190
Oh...

14:00.560 --> 14:01.820
I'll tell you when
we're a little closer

14:01.820 --> 14:04.570
I'll tell you when
we're a little closer

14:01.880 --> 14:04.570
<i>He doesn't feel like explaining, huh?!</i>

14:05.940 --> 14:06.700
I want us to be closer

14:10.760 --> 14:12.080
You're so cute.

14:12.080 --> 14:15.980
<i>That's the sign I taught him last time.</i>

14:17.460 --> 14:21.460
There are several different
gestures for "cute."

14:17.750 --> 14:20.860
<i>There are several different 
gestures for "cute."</i>

14:20.860 --> 14:21.460
Mmm.

14:22.070 --> 14:23.460
<i>Such as "cute,"</i>

14:24.040 --> 14:26.210
<i>and "cute."</i>

14:26.210 --> 14:29.460
Wow... Any others?

14:31.240 --> 14:32.550
<i>Well...</i>

14:33.270 --> 14:35.720
<i>It's, uh...</i>

14:35.720 --> 14:39.480
Patting the head

14:36.160 --> 14:39.480
<i>The thing you always do...</i>

14:44.340 --> 14:47.360
The world of sign language is fascinating.

14:51.600 --> 14:53.900
When I first met you

14:54.620 --> 14:57.120
and I saw you signing,

14:57.830 --> 15:01.880
it felt like the world I'd lived in so far 
had been flipped upside down.

15:03.130 --> 15:05.880
I used to live overseas,

15:06.440 --> 15:09.750
and I naturally gained an interest 
in cultures and languages.

15:10.720 --> 15:13.800
They became my driving force in life,

15:14.450 --> 15:16.860
and I kept looking at goals 
far away in the distance.

15:17.790 --> 15:21.140
But you helped me realize 
that there were things close by, too.

15:25.120 --> 15:27.890
<i>Huh? Was he saying something?</i>

15:27.890 --> 15:29.830
Do you want to get to know me better?

15:31.950 --> 15:35.200
Yes! I want us to be closer,
much more than now

15:34.390 --> 15:35.960
What's the sign for "more"?

15:43.430 --> 15:44.730
<i>More.</i>

15:47.280 --> 15:48.550
<i>More...</i>

15:50.070 --> 15:51.170
<i>and more...</i>

15:52.120 --> 15:53.430
<i>and more...</i>

15:53.430 --> 15:54.330
<i>and mo—</i>

16:07.680 --> 16:10.400
Okay, I hear ya.

16:13.240 --> 16:18.910
<i>While he holds my hands, I feel like 
I'm dancing upon the palm of his.</i>

16:19.540 --> 16:23.920
<i>His carefree attitude only makes 
my heart race even more.</i>

16:25.000 --> 16:25.860
<i>Wha?</i>

16:26.530 --> 16:27.820
<i>Why?</i>

16:28.840 --> 16:30.810
Du bist süß.

16:40.820 --> 16:44.060
<i>H-He's messing with me to see how I'll react?!</i>

16:45.480 --> 16:49.570
<i>But that's fine, as long as it makes him smile.</i>

16:50.900 --> 16:57.190
<i>Itsuomi-san's fingers hold on to me, 
as though to say they won't let me go.</i>

16:57.910 --> 17:01.720
<i>And all I can do is cling on to them tight.</i>

17:02.470 --> 17:05.610
<i>It's almost painful, 
but it still doesn't feel real.</i>

17:07.220 --> 17:10.740
<i>A little over an hour until curfew.</i>

17:11.970 --> 17:15.930
<i>The snow falling outside seemed 
to freeze in place for a moment,</i>

17:16.720 --> 17:18.790
<i>but that was only wishful thinking on my part.</i>

17:24.740 --> 17:26.810
Still snowing, huh?

17:27.600 --> 17:28.860
I love the snow

17:32.120 --> 17:33.700
Is that the sign for snow?

17:34.440 --> 17:35.990
I love it too, just like you.

17:35.990 --> 17:41.990
<b>I love it just like you</b>

17:36.330 --> 17:39.180
<i>I know he's not talking about loving me!</i>

17:39.760 --> 17:41.240
What's the sign language for "love"?

17:45.900 --> 17:48.300
This? I'll use it someday.

17:48.300 --> 17:49.160
<i>Huh?!</i>

17:52.420 --> 17:54.510
On whom?

17:52.870 --> 17:54.510
Oh, I mean, like,

17:55.020 --> 17:57.010
"I love traveling" and stuff.

17:57.010 --> 18:03.520
<b>Clean  Easy  Convenient     From washing to drying, non-stop!!</b>

17:57.010 --> 18:03.520
<b>Laundromat</b>

17:59.140 --> 18:01.340
I'll walk you. Which way to your home?

18:15.560 --> 18:17.280
<i>The pedestrian side...</i>

18:18.050 --> 18:19.260
Don't get run over.

18:23.280 --> 18:26.600
<i>It may feel like he's got me 
wrapped around his fingers,</i>

18:26.600 --> 18:29.180
<i>but right now, he makes me feel safe.</i>

18:29.760 --> 18:34.250
<i>Anyone would fall for him 
if he treated them this way.</i>

18:36.550 --> 18:39.970
Is the lady who came
to your bar the other
night your girlfriend?

18:37.510 --> 18:38.170
Hm?

18:39.110 --> 18:39.970
Who?

18:42.680 --> 18:45.680
Two people came in really
drunk, and the guy with her
was wearing sunglasses

18:43.670 --> 18:45.680
Oh, them?

18:46.160 --> 18:49.400
<i>Why are you supposed to make 
eye contact at times like these?</i>

18:49.400 --> 18:51.210
<i>It's almost cruel.</i>

18:54.470 --> 18:57.360
I don't have a girlfriend. 
Emma's just a friend.

18:59.320 --> 19:00.360
<i>But...</i>

19:01.080 --> 19:03.640
<i>I'm sure she thinks differently.</i>

19:05.080 --> 19:06.120
How about you?

19:06.620 --> 19:10.650
What about that guy I saw you 
signing happily with at college?

19:11.050 --> 19:12.130
<i>Wait...</i>

19:12.920 --> 19:15.000
<i>He saw us back then?</i>

19:15.250 --> 19:19.090
Just a childhood friend

19:17.010 --> 19:19.130
We just somehow ended up
going to the same school
and college

19:19.090 --> 19:22.640
He picked up sign language
from his older sister,
who was learning it

19:19.810 --> 19:22.640
Huh... When was that?

19:22.890 --> 19:26.640
The first thing he ever
signed to me was
"You fool!" It was back
in 2nd grade.

19:22.920 --> 19:24.890
<i>You fool!</i>

19:28.280 --> 19:29.130
Oh.

19:29.640 --> 19:33.350
We usually don't ever interact.

19:31.590 --> 19:33.640
Enough of this topic.

19:33.640 --> 19:35.650
<i>Whimsical as ever, I see.</i>

19:35.650 --> 19:35.980
We usually don't ever interact.

19:35.940 --> 19:37.530
When can I see you next?

19:38.530 --> 19:42.280
Hmm... Rockin' Robin is closed on Mondays.

19:44.420 --> 19:46.780
Let me guess. Does that mean "promise"?

19:57.250 --> 19:57.550
<b>swing</b>

19:57.670 --> 19:57.960
<b>swing</b>

19:58.090 --> 19:58.380
<b>swing</b>

19:58.500 --> 19:58.800
<b>swing</b>

19:58.920 --> 19:59.210
<b>swing</b>

19:59.340 --> 19:59.590
<b>swing</b>

20:05.560 --> 20:06.550
Let's go home.

20:11.120 --> 20:13.340
<i>Snow fills the sky above.</i>

20:13.890 --> 20:16.080
<i>It blows with the wind,</i>

20:16.080 --> 20:19.030
<i>just like my heart letting off steam right now.</i>

20:20.020 --> 20:22.340
<i>How childish can I be?</i>

20:23.440 --> 20:25.340
<i>I don't want to say goodbye.</i>

20:32.690 --> 20:34.780
Uh, how long have you been there?

20:34.780 --> 20:36.880
Just got here. And I bought some booze.

20:37.670 --> 20:40.130
Itsu-kun, let me stay the night.

20:43.660 --> 20:46.410
I only let you stay last time 
because Shin was there, too.

20:46.410 --> 20:47.800
I know that.

20:50.960 --> 20:54.290
You get where I'm going with this, don't you?

20:54.290 --> 20:55.770
Get off of me.

21:01.490 --> 21:02.550
Come in, I guess.

21:08.240 --> 21:10.280
What'll you have?

21:10.280 --> 21:11.120
I'm good.

21:11.120 --> 21:12.220
Huh?

21:12.220 --> 21:14.870
Feel free to use whatever.

21:15.240 --> 21:18.000
Spare key's by the entrance. 
Do not give it to Shin.

21:18.000 --> 21:19.130
Wait!

21:21.140 --> 21:23.150
Where are you going?

21:23.150 --> 21:26.560
It's late and it's snowing, so stay inside.

21:26.560 --> 21:28.890
Are you that put off by my showing up?

21:29.590 --> 21:31.390
Don't pull this crap anymore.

21:31.390 --> 21:32.970
What...

21:33.300 --> 21:35.680
I'm only doing this because it's you!

21:35.680 --> 21:36.630
Emma.

21:37.400 --> 21:41.030
Don't wail by my front door. 
You'll bother the neighbors.

21:41.030 --> 21:42.400
Meanie!

21:43.480 --> 21:47.830
Sheesh! Who leaves a girl alone in their home?!

21:47.830 --> 21:51.240
Yeah, yeah, I'll leave! 
Once I finish this drink...

21:52.990 --> 21:56.550
Itsu-kun, you jerk!

21:56.550 --> 21:57.640
Ah!

21:58.500 --> 22:00.500
<b>Sign</b>

22:03.000 --> 22:06.010
<b>Sign Language Guide</b>

22:03.750 --> 22:05.610
"Sign Language Guide"?

22:06.430 --> 22:08.460
What... is this?

23:15.030 --> 23:30.260
What Kind of Voice
